IMPORT prelude

-- Foreign Interference (Countermeasures) Act 2021 (Singapore) -- who is a "foreigner" and a "foreign principal" (s 4), who is a
-- politically significant person (s 14), the clandestine-interference offences and their penalties (ss 17 to 19), penalties for
-- ignoring a Part 3 direction (s 45), and the political-donation rules an ordinary donor or recipient meets: reportable donations
-- (s 53), permissible donors (s 55), impermissible and anonymous donations (ss 56 to 58), return within the grace period (s 60),
-- the major political donor report (s 70), donating on behalf of others (s 72), knowing acceptance (s 75(5)), and a citizen's
-- declaration of foreign political membership (ss 79, 86(2)).
--
-- Edition: Act No. 28 of 2021, informal consolidation (version in force from 8/12/2025), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/FICA2021.txt (retrieved 1 October 2026, "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026"). The latest amendment
-- annotated in the body is Act 30 of 2024 wef 01/11/2024; Act 8 of 2023 (wef 01/06/2023, 29/12/2023, 14/06/2024) and Act 29 of
-- 2022 are also annotated. The arrangement of sections at the top of the deposit is out of step with the body; the body's section
-- numbers are followed here.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0059 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. SCOPED to the provisions an ordinary person, donor or small organisation meets. Not encoded: the Minister's
-- authorisations and the content of each Part 3 direction (ss 20 to 38), proscribed online locations (ss 39 to 41), designation of
-- Part 4 persons (ss 47 to 49), the meaning of "political donation" in detail (ss 51, 52), donation-report contents, timing and
-- declarations (ss 62 to 66), the stepped-up directives (ss 67 to 69, 71, 81 to 85, 88 to 91), foreign-affiliation reports by
-- politically significant persons (ss 76 to 78), false reports (ss 74, 87), appeals and Reviewing Tribunals (ss 92 to 104), and
-- administration and enforcement (ss 105 onwards). Amounts "or a higher amount prescribed by Regulations in substitution" are
-- encoded at the figure in the Act; no Regulations were retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Foreign Interference (Countermeasures) Act 2021`

§§ `4 -- foreigner and foreign principal`

-- s 4: "foreigner" means "an individual who is not a citizen of Singapore". "foreign principal" means (a) a foreigner; (b) a foreign
-- government; (c) a foreign government-related individual; (d) a foreign legislature; (e) a foreign political organisation; (f) a
-- foreign public enterprise; or (g) a foreign business (an entity constituted under a foreign law or with its principal place of
-- business in a foreign country, "even if incorporated under any written law").
-- A permanent resident is not a citizen, so is a foreigner and a foreign principal. That follows from the words; the Act has no
-- separate category for permanent residents.
DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    `a Singapore citizen`
    `a Singapore permanent resident`
    `a foreign national`
    `a foreign government`
    `a foreign political party`
    `a company with its principal place of business abroad`
    `a Singapore company doing business in Singapore`

GIVEN `the actor` IS AN Actor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the actor is a foreign principal` IF
    CONSIDER `the actor`
    WHEN `a Singapore citizen` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a Singapore company doing business in Singapore` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `14 -- politically significant persons`

-- s 14: "politically significant person" means (a) a political party; (b) a candidate; (c) an election agent of a candidate; (d) a
-- political office holder; (e) a Member of Parliament; (f) a member of the executive committee of a political party (a "senior
-- political party official"); (g) a Part 4 politically significant person (an entity or individual designated under s 47(1) or
-- 48(1)). Part 5 directives (ss 67, 68) can be given to a Part 4 person: here a Part 4 person is listed by which directive it has.
DECLARE Recipient IS ONE OF
    `a political party`
    `a candidate`
    `an election agent`
    `a political office holder`
    `a Member of Parliament who is not an office holder`
    `a senior political party official`
    `a designated person with no directive`
    `a designated person with an anonymous donations directive`
    `a designated person with a prohibited donor directive`
    `a private individual`

GIVEN `the recipient` IS A Recipient
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the recipient is politically significant` IF
    CONSIDER `the recipient`
    WHEN `a private individual` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `17 to 19 -- clandestine foreign interference by electronic communications`

-- s 17(1): an offence if Y (a) undertakes electronic communications activity "that results in or involves publishing in Singapore";
-- (b) on behalf of a foreign principal (or someone acting for one); (c) "knows or has reason to believe" the activity or material is
-- or is likely to be prejudicial to security, public health, safety, tranquillity or finances, or to friendly relations, incites
-- enmity between groups, diminishes public confidence in the Government, or is directed towards a political end in Singapore; and
-- (d) any part of it "is covert or involves deception". (3): individual $50,000 or 7 years or both; otherwise $500,000.
-- s 18(1): the same (a), (b); (c) Z "intends" to influence a targeted person to act in one of those ways; (d) Z "conceals from, or
-- fails to disclose to, the targeted person" the foreign link. (3): individual $100,000 or 14 years or both; otherwise $1 million.
-- s 19: preparing or planning: for s 17, individual $30,000 or 5 years, otherwise $300,000; for s 18, individual $60,000 or 9 years,
-- otherwise $600,000.
-- No element requires the material to be false. Open, disclosed foreign-funded publishing falls outside s 17 for want of (d).
GIVEN `publishes in Singapore electronically` IS A BOOLEAN, `acts on behalf of a foreign principal` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knows or has reason to believe it is harmful or political` IS A BOOLEAN, `covert or deceptive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is a section 17 offence` IF
        `publishes in Singapore electronically`
    AND `acts on behalf of a foreign principal`
    AND `knows or has reason to believe it is harmful or political`
    AND `covert or deceptive`

GIVEN `publishes in Singapore electronically` IS A BOOLEAN, `acts on behalf of a foreign principal` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `intends to influence a target to act harmfully or politically` IS A BOOLEAN, `hides the foreign link from the target` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is a section 18 offence` IF
        `publishes in Singapore electronically`
    AND `acts on behalf of a foreign principal`
    AND `intends to influence a target to act harmfully or politically`
    AND `hides the foreign link from the target`

DECLARE Interference IS ONE OF
    `section 17 interference`
    `section 18 targeted interference`
    `preparing section 17 interference`
    `preparing section 18 interference`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Interference, `the offender is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `section 17 interference` THEN IF `the offender is an individual` THEN 50000 ELSE 500000
    WHEN `section 18 targeted interference` THEN IF `the offender is an individual` THEN 100000 ELSE 1000000
    WHEN `preparing section 17 interference` THEN IF `the offender is an individual` THEN 30000 ELSE 300000
    WHEN `preparing section 18 interference` THEN IF `the offender is an individual` THEN 60000 ELSE 600000

-- A body that is not an individual cannot be imprisoned; 0 years for it.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Interference, `the offender is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in years` MEANS
    IF NOT `the offender is an individual` THEN 0
    ELSE CONSIDER `the offence`
         WHEN `section 17 interference` THEN 7
         WHEN `section 18 targeted interference` THEN 14
         WHEN `preparing section 17 interference` THEN 5
         WHEN `preparing section 18 interference` THEN 9

§§ `45 -- failing to comply with a Part 3 direction`

-- s 45(1): an offence to fail "without reasonable excuse" to comply with a Part 3 direction, "whether in or outside Singapore".
-- (2) stop communication (end-user), Class 1 must-carry, disgorgement, or technical assistance to a proprietor: individual $20,000 or
-- 2 years. (3) Class 2 or 3 must-carry, remedial must-carry, account restriction, disabling, service restriction, or technical
-- assistance to anyone else: individual $20,000 or 12 months "and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not
-- exceeding $100,000 for every day" (otherwise $1 million and $100,000 a day). (4) Class 4 must-carry: individual $40,000 or 4
-- years. (5) access blocking or app removal: "$20,000 for every day ... but not exceeding in total $500,000".
-- (6): it is NOT a defence that a contract or other law forbids compliance, or that an appeal is pending.
DECLARE Direction IS ONE OF
    `a stop communication direction`
    `a disgorgement direction`
    `an account restriction direction`
    `a disabling direction`
    `a Class 4 must-carry direction`

GIVEN `the direction` IS A Direction
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for an individual who ignores it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the direction`
    WHEN `a Class 4 must-carry direction` THEN 40000
    OTHERWISE 20000

GIVEN `the direction` IS A Direction
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the further daily fine for an individual who keeps ignoring it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the direction`
    WHEN `an account restriction direction` THEN 100000
    WHEN `a disabling direction` THEN 100000
    OTHERWISE 0

-- s 45(5): $20,000 a day, capped at $500,000 in total.
GIVEN `days of non-compliance` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for ignoring an access blocking direction` MEANS
    IF `days of non-compliance` TIMES 20000 GREATER THAN 500000 THEN 500000 ELSE `days of non-compliance` TIMES 20000

§§ `55 -- permissible donors`

-- s 55(1): "permissible donor" means (a) "an individual who is a citizen of Singapore and is at least 21 years of age"; (c) "a
-- Singapore entity which carries on business wholly or mainly in Singapore and is not prohibited by written law or its own
-- constitution from donating" for a political end. A Singapore entity is a Singapore-controlled corporation (majority of directors
-- and members citizens), partnership or unincorporated association. (Bequests (b), voluntary labour (d), and party-to-candidate
-- donations (e), (f) are not modelled.)
DECLARE Donor HAS
    `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `age` IS A NUMBER
    `is Singapore-controlled` IS A BOOLEAN
    `carries on business wholly or mainly in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is barred from political donating by law or its constitution` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the donor` IS A Donor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the donor is permissible` IF
    IF `the donor`'s `is an individual`
    THEN `the donor`'s `is a citizen` AND `the donor`'s `age` AT LEAST 21
    ELSE     `the donor`'s `is Singapore-controlled`
         AND `the donor`'s `carries on business wholly or mainly in Singapore`
         AND (NOT `the donor`'s `is barred from political donating by law or its constitution`)

§§ `56 -- impermissible donors`

-- s 56: a politically significant person "must not accept any political donation" from a donor whom it knows (a) "is not a
-- permissible donor", or (b) for a Part 4 person, "is a prohibited donor ... because of a prohibited donor directive".
-- For a Part 4 person WITHOUT a prohibited donor directive, (a) does not apply: it may take money from a foreigner.
GIVEN `the recipient` IS A Recipient, `the donor` IS A Donor, `the donor is named in a prohibited donor directive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the recipient must refuse the donation` IF
    CONSIDER `the recipient`
    WHEN `a private individual` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a designated person with no directive` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a designated person with an anonymous donations directive` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a designated person with a prohibited donor directive` THEN `the donor is named in a prohibited donor directive`
    OTHERWISE NOT `the donor is permissible` `the donor`

§§ `57, 58 -- anonymous donations`

-- s 57: (a) every politically significant person other than a Part 4 person, and (b) a Part 4 person given an anonymous donations
-- directive, "must not accept any political donation that is an anonymous donation". s 58(1): despite s 57 it may accept, in each
-- relevant period, anonymous political donations "which in total are LESS THAN the applicable cap". (2) the cap is $5,000 for (a) a
-- political party, candidate or election agent, (b) a political office holder, (c) a Member of Parliament who is not an office
-- holder, (d) a Part 4 person given an anonymous donations directive.
-- A senior political party official is barred by s 57(a) but has NO cap in s 58(2). Reading the words, it may accept no anonymous
-- donation at all. That is an inference from the omission; the Act does not say so expressly.
GIVEN `the recipient` IS A Recipient, `anonymous total already accepted this period` IS A NUMBER, `this anonymous donation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the recipient may accept the anonymous donation` IF
    CONSIDER `the recipient`
    WHEN `a private individual` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a designated person with no directive` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a designated person with a prohibited donor directive` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a senior political party official` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE `anonymous total already accepted this period` PLUS `this anonymous donation` LESS THAN 5000

§§ `53 -- reportable political donations`

-- s 53(1): a "reportable political donation" is "a political donation of or exceeding $10,000". (2): a smaller donation is treated as
-- reportable if it and "another earlier, separate political donation made by that donor to the same politically significant person
-- within the same reporting period" would, "if aggregated", reach that amount.
GIVEN `this donation` IS A NUMBER, `earlier donations by the same donor this period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the donation is reportable` IF
    `this donation` PLUS `earlier donations by the same donor this period` AT LEAST 10000

§§ `60 -- returning a donation within the grace period`

-- s 60(2): a donation the recipient is prohibited from accepting, or decides to refuse, must within the grace period be sent back
-- (or an equivalent sum sent) to the donor, or for an anonymous donation dealt with under s 59. (3): the "grace period" is "a period
-- of 30 days starting the date when the donation is so received". Read literally, the day of receipt is day 1, so the last day is
-- the day of receipt plus 29. (Days are numbered; calendar dates are not modelled.)
-- (4): an offence where a prohibited donation is not returned by the end of the grace period and the recipient "knows or is reckless
-- as to whether" it is prohibited. Fine up to $5,000 or 12 months, plus a continuing daily fine of $500 for a party or Part 4 entity
-- and $200 for a candidate or anyone else.
GIVEN `day received` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day to return the donation` MEANS `day received` PLUS 29

GIVEN `the donation was prohibited` IS A BOOLEAN, `returned within the grace period` IS A BOOLEAN, `knew or was reckless` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `keeping the donation is a section 60 offence` IF
    `the donation was prohibited` AND (NOT `returned within the grace period`) AND `knew or was reckless`

GIVEN `the recipient` IS A Recipient
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the further daily fine under section 60` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the recipient`
    WHEN `a political party` THEN 500
    WHEN `a designated person with no directive` THEN 500
    WHEN `a designated person with an anonymous donations directive` THEN 500
    WHEN `a designated person with a prohibited donor directive` THEN 500
    OTHERWISE 200

-- s 60(4)(d) gives $500 a day for a "Part 4 politically significant ENTITY"; a designated individual falls in (f) at $200. This
-- encoding does not distinguish designated entities from designated individuals, and takes the entity figure.

§§ `75(5) -- accepting from an impermissible donor`

-- s 75(5): a politically significant person who accepts a donation from an impermissible or prohibited donor, and "knew or ought
-- reasonably to have known" it, is liable to $10,000 or 12 months or both, "and, in the case of a second or subsequent offence, to a
-- fine not exceeding $20,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or to both".
GIVEN `a second or subsequent offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under section 75(5)` MEANS IF `a second or subsequent offence` THEN 20000 ELSE 10000

§§ `70 -- major political donor report`

-- s 70(1): a person "(not being a politically significant person)" who in any single year makes donations "all of which are accepted
-- by or on behalf of any one of" (i) a political party or (ii) a Part 4 person given a prohibited donor directive, totalling "not less
-- than the threshold reporting value" ($10,000, (4)), must disclose them by 31 January of the following year ((2)(b)(i)). (5): fine
-- up to $5,000 and $500 a day continuing. s 71 lets a directive extend s 70 to donors to a Part 4 entity (not modelled).
-- Giving to a candidate or a Member of Parliament does not trigger s 70, however large.
GIVEN `the donor is politically significant` IS A BOOLEAN, `the recipient` IS A Recipient, `total given to that recipient this year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the donor must file a major political donor report` IF
        (NOT `the donor is politically significant`)
    AND `total given to that recipient this year` AT LEAST 10000
    AND CONSIDER `the recipient`
        WHEN `a political party` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a designated person with a prohibited donor directive` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `72 -- donating on behalf of others`

-- s 72(1): where a person causes a donation to be received "on behalf of" others, "each individual contribution ... is taken to be a
-- separate donation by that person". (2), (3): the principal donor or agent must give the recipient each real donor's details at
-- the time of receipt. (4): failing "without reasonable excuse" is an offence, fine up to $5,000.
GIVEN `passed on donations from others` IS A BOOLEAN, `gave each donor's details` IS A BOOLEAN, `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the collector commits a section 72 offence` IF
    `passed on donations from others` AND (NOT `gave each donor's details`) AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`)

§§ `79, 86(2) -- a citizen's foreign political membership`

-- s 79(1): "An individual who is a citizen of Singapore (and whether or not resident in Singapore)" must give a written declaration
-- within the prescribed time if he or she is or becomes "a member of a foreign legislature or a foreign political organisation".
-- (4): "member" includes an honorary member, but not a person "by reason only of being" (a) an employee, (b) a regular participant in
-- its activities, (c) a regular donor, or (d) a lobbyist for it. s 86(2): late declaration, fine up to $5,000 and $200 a day.
-- The duty is on every citizen, not only politically significant persons.
DECLARE Tie IS ONE OF
    `full member`
    `honorary member`
    `employee only`
    `regular participant only`
    `regular donor only`
    `lobbyist only`

GIVEN `is a citizen` IS A BOOLEAN, `the tie` IS A Tie
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a foreign membership declaration is required` IF
    `is a citizen` AND
        CONSIDER `the tie`
        WHEN `full member` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `honorary member` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
